---
description: graphify knowledge graph context — query first for token optimization
alwaysApply: true
---

This project has a graphify knowledge graph at `graphify-out/`. Use it as persistent memory so prompts do not re-scan the repo.

**On every prompt / run:** before Read, Grep, Glob, or exploratory Shell, query the graph:

- `graphify query "<question>" --budget 1500` — scoped subgraph
- `graphify path "<A>" "<B>"` — dependency path between two symbols
- `graphify explain "<concept>"` — neighbors of one concept

Pass this rule into every subagent that explores code. Do not skip graphify because files feel "already known."

Only use Read/Grep/Glob when:

1. graphify already oriented you and you need specific lines to edit or debug
2. `graphify-out/graph.json` does not exist yet

**After every code change:** run `graphify update . --no-cluster` (AST only, no API cost). Git post-commit/post-checkout hooks and Cursor `afterFileEdit`/`stop` hooks should do this automatically; if they did not, run it yourself before finishing.

- Prefer query/path/explain over reading `GRAPH_REPORT.md`
- Read `graphify-out/GRAPH_REPORT.md` only for a broad architecture review
- If `graphify-out/wiki/index.md` exists, navigate it instead of raw files
